  "note": "Triennial election of the Ballycastle Urban District Council, polled Wednesday 17 May 1967. Twenty-one candidates contested twelve seats; the Unionists gained a seat. The new council was five Nationalists, four N.D.P., two Unionists and one Independent (Belfast News-Letter, 19 May 1967, pp. 12 and 14). Archie M'Auley was a new member."
